---
# The root config, minus one check that does not fit test code.
InheritParentConfig: true

Checks: >
  -bugprone-unchecked-optional-access

# A test asserts a thing exists and then reads it:
#
#   REQUIRE(outcome.assigned_name.has_value());
#   CHECK(*outcome.assigned_name == "x");
#
# The guard is a doctest macro, which the check cannot see through, so all 13
# instances are false positives. Suppressing them one by one would bury what the
# tests actually say — and if the assumption is ever wrong, the REQUIRE above fails
# and names the line, which is the whole point of writing it that way.
#
# The check stays on for src/, where a failed guess crashes instead.
